# What `docker build .` is allowed to send the daemon. Without this file the
# context is the whole working tree — on a developer's laptop that is ~109 MB,
# almost all of it webui/node_modules, plus whatever untracked binaries and
# databases a day's work left lying around. CI never noticed because a fresh
# checkout has none of it.
#
# Two of these entries are correctness rather than speed:
#
#   - .env. It is gitignored, so it only ever exists on a laptop, and `COPY . .`
#     in the build stage would bake a developer's real credentials into an image
#     layer — where `docker history` can read them back out even though the
#     runtime stage never copies the file forward.
#   - webui/node_modules. The ui stage runs `npm ci` and then `COPY webui/ ./`,
#     which would overwrite the tree npm just installed with whatever a laptop
#     happens to have. The lockfile stops being the thing that decides.
#
# Patterns here are matched against the context root, so `dist` is this
# repository's dist and not, say, webui/dist.

# Secrets. Mirrors .gitignore; .env.example is documentation and carries no
# values, but nothing in the build reads it either.
.env
.env.*
*.creds
*.pem

# Version control and CI. Nothing in the build shells out to git — the
# Dockerfile takes VERSION/COMMIT/DATE as build args precisely so it does not
# have to — so .git is weight and nothing else.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Build output. dist/ is GoReleaser's, web/ is the vite bundle (the ui stage
# rebuilds it from source), and the two bare binaries are what `make build`
# leaves at the root.
dist
bin
web
/central-config
/testconsole
*.exe
*.test
*.out

# Dependencies that are installed rather than copied.
node_modules
webui/node_modules

# Local databases from the SQLite test stack.
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Coverage, editor and OS noise.
coverage.*
*.cover
*.coverprofile
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea
.vscode
*.swp

# Documentation and deployment manifests. LICENSE and README.md stay: they are
# not in the image either, but they are small and their absence is the sort of
# thing that breaks a later `COPY LICENSE` with a confusing error.
docs
deploy
migrations
CHANGELOG.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md
SECURITY.md
Makefile
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
.goreleaser.yaml
.golangci.yml
.editorconfig
